# Built dashboard bundle — never line-ending-converted.
#
# The VM consumes static/dashboard/ byte-for-byte, and the deploy runbook
# verifies "VM == brafter" by comparing sha256 against the committed blob.
# With core.autocrlf=true on a Windows checkout and no .gitattributes, git
# classified the minified bundle as text and rewrote LF -> CRLF during
# `git archive`, so the artefact that reached the VM silently differed from
# the one that was committed and reviewed — on every deploy, not just one.
#
# The 7 rewrites landed inside JavaScript template literals in React's
# internals (component-stack splitting, `.replace(re, "\n")` normalisation),
# which is exactly the kind of damage that stays invisible until it isn't.
# -text disables both directions of conversion, so what is committed is what
# ships and the sha256 check means something again.
security_scanner/static/dashboard/** -text
